{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2795 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "44deccc9b890583eb40a1c118499800419010923bf81cf3bcf55e19732c437f3" :edb/db-before-t 2794 :edb/db-after-t 2795 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536107 50 #inst "2026-10-09T15:10:26.194Z" 13194139536107 true] [17592186087491 1100 "Given that the asymptotes of the hyperbola below are $y=\\pm\\dfrac{5}{7}x,$ find the parametric equations of the hyperbola.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/assets/fd2618e961c15a9b0665e73e18544ab08b0d611b962bc3771558c61450cf49e5.png)" 13194139536107 true] [17592186087491 1100 "Given that the asymptotes of the hyperbola below are $y=\\pm\\dfrac{5}{7}x,$ find the parametric equations of the hyperbola.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/assets/fd2618e961c15a9b0665e73e18544ab08b0d611b962bc3771558c61450cf49e5.png)" 13194139536107 false] [17592186087581 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/assets/6e12d114aedfd6c5c8ab5830e052fcc1dd3c937b825665a0490b42ca0c87972c.png)\n\nThe quarter-hyperbola above is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx = \\sqrt2\\sec{t}, \\qquad y = \\sqrt3\\tan{t}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t?$" 13194139536107 true] [17592186087581 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/assets/6e12d114aedfd6c5c8ab5830e052fcc1dd3c937b825665a0490b42ca0c87972c.png)\n\nThe quarter-hyperbola above is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx = \\sqrt2\\sec{t}, \\qquad y = \\sqrt3\\tan{t}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t?$" 13194139536107 false] [17592186087581 1145 "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx= \\sqrt2 \\sec{t}, \\quad\ny = \\sqrt3 \\tan{t}, \\quad\nt \\in [-\\pi,\\pi], \\quad\nt \\neq \\pm\\dfrac{\\pi}2.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a quarter-hyperbola, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/assets/730325137cfca58eb17d65103e539d084f81d7ab810628261125c29dbb8a0284.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $\\left[0, \\dfrac{\\pi}2\\right)$ we get the required quarter-hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe the required quarter-hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx= \\sqrt2\\sec{t}, \\quad\ny = \\sqrt3\\tan{t}, \\quad\nt \\in \\left[0, \\dfrac{\\pi}2\\right).\n$$" 13194139536107 true] [17592186087581 1145 "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx= \\sqrt2 \\sec{t}, \\quad\ny = \\sqrt3 \\tan{t}, \\quad\nt \\in [-\\pi,\\pi], \\quad\nt \\neq \\pm\\dfrac{\\pi}2.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a quarter-hyperbola, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/assets/730325137cfca58eb17d65103e539d084f81d7ab810628261125c29dbb8a0284.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $\\left[0, \\dfrac{\\pi}2\\right)$ we get the required quarter-hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe the required quarter-hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx= \\sqrt2\\sec{t}, \\quad\ny = \\sqrt3\\tan{t}, \\quad\nt \\in \\left[0, \\dfrac{\\pi}2\\right).\n$$" 13194139536107 false] [17592186087681 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383900 13194139536107 true] [17592186087681 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383939 13194139536107 true] [17592186087681 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383945 13194139536107 true] [17592186087681 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383961 13194139536107 true] [17592186087681 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383968 13194139536107 true] [17592186087682 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383907 13194139536107 true] [17592186087682 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383951 13194139536107 true] [17592186087682 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383954 13194139536107 true] [17592186087682 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383958 13194139536107 true] [17592186087745 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383893 13194139536107 true] [17592186087745 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383928 13194139536107 true] [17592186087745 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383931 13194139536107 true] [17592186087745 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383934 13194139536107 true] [17592186087746 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383914 13194139536107 true] [17592186087746 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383921 13194139536107 true] [17592186088320 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536107 true] [17592186088320 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x = \\sqrt{5}\\sec t, y = 3\\tan t$." 13194139536107 false] [17592186088320 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$" 13194139536107 true] [17592186088320 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{5}} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{5} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{3} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536107 true] [17592186088392 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/assets/90b505954bb714ad86f60e07f7a26c16c954139689d96684ed553a7b494f0527.png)\n\nOne branch of a hyperbola (shown above) is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t?$" 13194139536107 true] [17592186088392 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064533/assets/90b505954bb714ad86f60e07f7a26c16c954139689d96684ed553a7b494f0527.png)\n\nOne branch of a hyperbola (shown above) is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t?$" 13194139536107 false] [17592186088392 1145 "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a single branch, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/assets/b43dcf6c343994e3226e2840a0ae80f60484c8de5d7984f61ec6447185181a76.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0]$ and $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ we get only the right branch.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe only the right branch are\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=7\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).\n$$" 13194139536107 true] [17592186088392 1145 "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a single branch, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064533/assets/b43dcf6c343994e3226e2840a0ae80f60484c8de5d7984f61ec6447185181a76.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0]$ and $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ we get only the right branch.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe only the right branch are\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=7\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).\n$$" 13194139536107 false] [17592186331441 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383938 13194139536107 true] [17592186331470 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/assets/5b133ac885861d82704a6d6c2d99b8e4179210e4f28e94bc6d7283da23f97042.png)\n\nThe quarter-hyperbola above is defined by the parametric equations \n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nDetermine the domain of the parameter $t$ for this quarter, assuming that the entire parabola is defined only for $t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$\n\n$t\\in [${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$)$" 13194139536107 true] [17592186331470 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/assets/5b133ac885861d82704a6d6c2d99b8e4179210e4f28e94bc6d7283da23f97042.png)\n\nThe quarter-hyperbola above is defined by the parametric equations \n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nDetermine the domain of the parameter $t$ for this quarter, assuming that the entire parabola is defined only for $t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$\n\n$t\\in [${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$)$" 13194139536107 false] [17592186331470 1145 "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a quarter-hyperbola, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/assets/6ac31692404208d80637291fb30be028a7efdc3a172af0337da26039f1e87326.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $[-\\pi ,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ we get only the quarter-hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe the required quarter-hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}).\n$$" 13194139536107 true] [17592186331470 1145 "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a quarter-hyperbola, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053984/assets/6ac31692404208d80637291fb30be028a7efdc3a172af0337da26039f1e87326.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $[-\\pi ,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ we get only the quarter-hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe the required quarter-hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}).\n$$" 13194139536107 false] [17592186335854 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/assets/a2f0f570ecc68de1a5b34fb3bd1b341fc83a728b026b035dde848dbf986e441b.png)\n\nThe quarter-hyperbola above is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t?$" 13194139536107 true] [17592186335854 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058380/assets/a2f0f570ecc68de1a5b34fb3bd1b341fc83a728b026b035dde848dbf986e441b.png)\n\nThe quarter-hyperbola above is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $t?$" 13194139536107 false] [17592186335854 1145 "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a quarter-hyperbola, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/assets/e7ef7fd90c828767359daf69f68f406d61e3f82ad86b1f6b3a9480c99dedadf8.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0],$ we get the quarter-hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe the required quarter-hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0].\n$$" 13194139536107 true] [17592186335854 1145 "The parametric equations of the full hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ],\\,t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a quarter-hyperbola, we refer to the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058380/assets/e7ef7fd90c828767359daf69f68f406d61e3f82ad86b1f6b3a9480c99dedadf8.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $t$ to $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0],$ we get the quarter-hyperbola.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations that describe the required quarter-hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,t\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0].\n$$" 13194139536107 false] [17592186383893 1017 #edb/ref 17592186383894 13194139536107 true] [17592186383893 1089 "q-106509" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383893 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536107 true] [17592186383893 1100 "What are the parametric equations of the hyperbola ${x}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1?$" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383893 1113 #uuid "6884465a-f493-5a74-9bcc-3f6f410be1b3" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383893 1145 "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=1$ and $b=\\sqrt{9}=3.$ Therefore, the parametric equations are\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383895 13194139536107 true] [17592186383894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383896 13194139536107 true] [17592186383894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383897 13194139536107 true] [17592186383894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383898 13194139536107 true] [17592186383894 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383899 13194139536107 true] [17592186383894 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536107 true] [17592186383894 1041 "selection" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383894 1104 #edb/ref 17592186383896 13194139536107 true] [17592186383894 1110 #uuid "a8450423-5d4c-55b6-a37d-5df5f56fa9f1" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383895 1034 "x=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\,y=9\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383895 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536107 true] [17592186383895 1111 #uuid "88d5b1a2-c295-5492-9a3f-d2fdf2d66a03" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383896 1034 "x=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\,y=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383896 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536107 true] [17592186383896 1111 #uuid "ecfd4d97-3120-5771-8fbd-7fcf0f80af97" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383897 1034 "x=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\,y=9\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383897 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536107 true] [17592186383897 1111 #uuid "6ffe50f9-71b9-562a-ab8b-dbc24079e866" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383898 1034 "x=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\,y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383898 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536107 true] [17592186383898 1111 #uuid "4cac0ca9-c280-56b2-9aaf-1acd7f0d4abb" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383899 1034 "x=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383899 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536107 true] [17592186383899 1111 #uuid "86d0c591-55a9-546a-87ed-dd1a175476f4" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383900 1017 #edb/ref 17592186383901 13194139536107 true] [17592186383900 1089 "q-106521" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383900 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536107 true] [17592186383900 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/assets/2fe325dcc61b0cec5483791e00842ca975b5d712ffed93cf48eacc52a6cd8daf.png)\n\nFind the parametric equations of the hyperbola shown above given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}x.$" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383900 1113 #uuid "a5eb140c-ede8-53b2-a8e6-2cb164c906ca" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383900 1145 "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(\\pm a,0).$ From the graph, we have that $(\\sqrt{2},0)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nThe asymptotes of a horizontal hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}x,$ and so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{b}{a} & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{b}{\\sqrt{2}} & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ b & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383901 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383902 13194139536107 true] [17592186383901 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383903 13194139536107 true] [17592186383901 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383904 13194139536107 true] [17592186383901 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383905 13194139536107 true] [17592186383901 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383906 13194139536107 true] [17592186383901 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536107 true] [17592186383901 1041 "selection" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383901 1104 #edb/ref 17592186383906 13194139536107 true] [17592186383901 1110 #uuid "db5aa961-bbd5-5c70-8665-0cfabeaa497c" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383902 1034 "x=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383902 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536107 true] [17592186383902 1111 #uuid "09cc1b11-c989-5980-918f-48988fe5a14e" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383903 1034 "x=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\,y=\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383903 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536107 true] [17592186383903 1111 #uuid "22c9d02d-8d94-5152-9fb1-c7e67d44d226" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383904 1034 "x=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\,y=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383904 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536107 true] [17592186383904 1111 #uuid "b135a810-260e-5ad9-b396-974ebc5a2415" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383905 1034 "x=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\,y=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383905 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536107 true] [17592186383905 1111 #uuid "bab9069e-4c6a-500c-a545-4252f130c0f0" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383906 1034 "x=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,\\,y=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383906 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536107 true] [17592186383906 1111 #uuid "8f15f4f6-ed7b-50f2-8eba-94c77cc30ed1" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383907 1017 #edb/ref 17592186383908 13194139536107 true] [17592186383907 1089 "q-106526" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383907 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536107 true] [17592186383907 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383907 1113 #uuid "d7d4ecc2-8bf0-5598-b6c5-b9b1ccfe056d" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383907 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{\\sqrt{5}} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{5})^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{5} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}+1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383908 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383909 13194139536107 true] [17592186383908 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383910 13194139536107 true] [17592186383908 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383911 13194139536107 true] [17592186383908 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383912 13194139536107 true] [17592186383908 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383913 13194139536107 true] [17592186383908 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536107 true] [17592186383908 1041 "selection" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383908 1104 #edb/ref 17592186383912 13194139536107 true] [17592186383908 1110 #uuid "df82d9ab-6205-5f2a-a674-dfb23d1ad195" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383909 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383909 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536107 true] [17592186383909 1111 #uuid "a6fb6a4f-c0d7-5522-b257-07d03e6b798f" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383910 1034 "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}=1" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383910 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536107 true] [175