83946 1110 #uuid "37726d90-f059-5d1f-8aac-307bde69e296" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383947 1034 "8" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383947 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536107 true] [17592186383947 1111 #uuid "b1915e45-4f4c-50dc-8534-a0d37627ec4d" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383948 1034 "\\sqrt{8}" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383948 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536107 true] [17592186383948 1111 #uuid "2d9bd640-3962-50e6-9934-32fc14cbb391" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383949 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383950 13194139536107 true] [17592186383949 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536107 true] [17592186383949 1041 "field-2" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383949 1104 #edb/ref 17592186383950 13194139536107 true] [17592186383949 1110 #uuid "162b741f-24ca-5dc9-9d61-cb89935c5b3a" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383950 1034 "\\sqrt{3}\\tan(t)" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383950 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536107 true] [17592186383950 1111 #uuid "45b20f53-55e7-52eb-87a2-4655f7ddaa4c" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383951 1017 #edb/ref 17592186383952 13194139536107 true] [17592186383951 1089 "q-325931" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383951 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536107 true] [17592186383951 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$=1$" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383951 1113 #uuid "ce6563f1-55ba-5c31-9507-ab4cb56ae82c" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383951 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{3}} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{2}} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{8} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}+1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383952 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383953 13194139536107 true] [17592186383952 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536107 true] [17592186383952 1041 "field-1" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383952 1104 #edb/ref 17592186383953 13194139536107 true] [17592186383952 1110 #uuid "053fcdb4-6606-5e8e-aa29-55d3ec2903d4" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383953 1034 "\\frac{x^2}{3}-\\frac{y^2}{8}" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383953 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536107 true] [17592186383953 1111 #uuid "2c86ca89-9d51-55f0-9d9b-7e9a1ca21565" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383954 1017 #edb/ref 17592186383955 13194139536107 true] [17592186383954 1089 "q-325932" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383954 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536107 true] [17592186383954 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=2\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$=1$" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383954 1113 #uuid "dffd576b-d9e4-51fa-bb28-71ffbae1e4ae" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383954 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{5}} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{5})^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{20} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{\\sqrt{7}} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{7})^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{7} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{7}+1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{20} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{20}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{7} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383955 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383956 13194139536107 true] [17592186383955 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383957 13194139536107 true] [17592186383955 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536107 true] [17592186383955 1041 "field-1" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383955 1104 #edb/ref 17592186383956 13194139536107 true] [17592186383955 1110 #uuid "21038133-0473-50e5-bcdb-5d60613e5317" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383956 1034 "\\frac{x^2}{20}-\\frac{y^2}{7}" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383956 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536107 true] [17592186383956 1111 #uuid "bdb1cb49-add0-569c-8932-ebbce9358326" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383957 1034 "\\frac{x^2}{10}-\\frac{y^2}{7}" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383957 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536107 true] [17592186383957 1111 #uuid "f4333225-e404-593e-8291-3d456cc5ed09" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383958 1017 #edb/ref 17592186383959 13194139536107 true] [17592186383958 1089 "q-325938" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383958 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536107 true] [17592186383958 1100 "Find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola $x=4\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=7\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$=1$" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383958 1113 #uuid "6bacdf2c-490b-532d-a769-2a66216dd8fe" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383958 1145 "To find the Cartesian equation of the hyperbola, we need to eliminate the parameter $t.$ We can do this using the secant-tangent identity.\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{sec}⁡t$ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{x}{4} & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & ={sec}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Isolating the $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t$ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =7\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{y}{7} & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{7}^{2}} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{49} & ={tan}^{2}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the two equations into the identity ${tan}^{2}⁡t+1={sec}^{2}⁡t$ and rearranging, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{tan}^{2}⁡t+1 & ={sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}+1 & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383959 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383960 13194139536107 true] [17592186383959 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536107 true] [17592186383959 1041 "field-1" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383959 1104 #edb/ref 17592186383960 13194139536107 true] [17592186383959 1110 #uuid "e7011158-217e-575a-b3d1-258d0960c19f" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383960 1034 "\\frac{x^2}{16}-\\frac{y^2}{49}" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383960 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536107 true] [17592186383960 1111 #uuid "d1ac7f6f-8694-5a63-a579-010534e0d10e" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383961 1017 #edb/ref 17592186383962 13194139536107 true] [17592186383961 1089 "q-7979" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383961 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536107 true] [17592186383961 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14077122/assets/c51295239ec195b494cfc67e295c50a7f1a9464bc0d24e32d53fb624f311cfdd.png)\n\nFind the parametric equations of the hyperbola shown above given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}x.$" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383961 1113 #uuid "eb7979ae-d137-50fb-a592-8def86946ad4" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383961 1145 "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(\\pm a,0).$ From the graph, we have that $(2,0)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=2.$\n\nThe asymptotes of a horizontal hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}x,$ and so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{b}{a} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{b}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ b & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383962 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383963 13194139536107 true] [17592186383962 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383964 13194139536107 true] [17592186383962 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383965 13194139536107 true] [17592186383962 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383966 13194139536107 true] [17592186383962 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383967 13194139536107 true] [17592186383962 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536107 true] [17592186383962 1041 "selection" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383962 1104 #edb/ref 17592186383965 13194139536107 true] [17592186383962 1110 #uuid "31a5318a-fadd-5fb4-ae35-a51222b3e5ad" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383963 1034 "x=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383963 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536107 true] [17592186383963 1111 #uuid "37ba290b-1fb7-50e0-a4f0-8063a348fb8d" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383964 1034 "x=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t" 13194139536107 true] [17592186383964 11